urrently  on sale on Amazon for only $2,100 with  prime shipping we'll leave a link down  below  now the 5k iMac starts at a base price  of only eighteen hundred dollars and you  get a similar six core processor in  faster graphics but I would highly  recommend paying the extra hundred  dollars for the SSD and updating the ram  yourself to a total of 40 gigabytes by  using the link below for only a hundred  and sixty-five dollars instead of  getting a total of 32 gigabytes from  Apple for $600 that's four hundred and  thirty-five dollars cheaper for even  more RAM that brings the total price of  the 5k IMAX to 2,000 $65 a bit less than  the MacBook Pro on sale  comparing Geekbench for multi-core  results the MacBook Pro is actually  slightly faster and comparing graphics  performance the iMac is over twice as  fast so you will see a big difference in  graphically intensive tasks and this  time the base iMac gets quick sync  technology but it still lacks the t2  chips HEV C encoding that comes with the  MacBook Pro either way unless you're  doing something graphically intensive  like video editing you really won't  notice much of a difference in  performance so the MacBook becomes a  really great value at the base price  thanks to its portability in the end it  really comes down to whether you want to  be portable or you want that beautiful  5k display if you enjoyed this  comparison click that button above the  sub and also check out some of our other  videos right there thanks for watching  and we'll see you in the next video  [Music]
 

